OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F308A1786652305
OL,3,CUK could see hottest day of year as
OL,4,Cparts of England may hit 38C
OL,6,FIt comes after Prime Minister Andy
OL,7,FBurnham chaired a meeting of the
OL,8,FGovernment's emergency Cobra committee
OL,9,Fon Wednesday in response to the
OL,10,Fprolonged spell of exceptionally hot
OL,11,Fand dry weather.
OL,13,FMet Office forecaster Alex Burkill
OL,14,Fsaid: "Temperatures (in areas covered
OL,15,Fby the amber warning) could reach
OL,16,Fhighs of around 36, 37, possibly 38C.
OL,26,@vD@GOU
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G2/10
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,309,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30803
SC,0003
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F308A1786652305
OL,3,CUK could see hottest day of year as
OL,4,Cparts of England may hit 38C
OL,6,F"Now when you get these sorts of high
OL,7,Ftemperatures, well that's when we
OL,8,Fcould see impacts to our
OL,9,Finfrastructure, our railway lines, our
OL,10,Froads, they are not designed for this
OL,11,Fsort of heat.
OL,13,F"And more people are likely to be
OL,14,Fimpacted by how hot it is with regards
OL,15,Fto their health."
OL,26,@nD@AOUuD@AOUwD@QO]
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G3/10
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
